  "topic": "Read and write Qaf (ق) at the beginning, middle and end of words, with Fatha, Kasra and Damma.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "learn": [
    {
      "en": "This is Qaf. A deep 'K' sound from the very back of the throat — no English equivalent!",
      "title": "Meet Qaf!",
      "ar": "ق",
      "aud": "c-0-ar",
      "tr": "Qaf"
    },
    {
      "en": "Like a circle with TWO dots above it. The two dots are Qaf's signature! The letter Qaf has two dots above it, and its sound comes from deep in the throat, like the letter Q.",
      "title": "How to write Qaf"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a fatha, Qaf says “qa”.",
      "title": "Qaf with fatha",
      "ar": "قَ",
      "aud": "c-2-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a kasra, Qaf says “qe”.",
      "title": "Qaf with kasra",
      "ar": "قِ",
      "aud": "c-3-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a damma, Qaf says “qo”.",
      "title": "Qaf with damma",
      "ar": "قُ",
      "aud": "c-4-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "“The Quran is the word of Allah”",
      "title": "Sentence of the lesson",
      "ar": "القُرْآنُ كَلَامُ اللَّهِ",
      "aud": "c-5-ar",
      "tr": "Al-Quranu Kalamu Allah"
    }
